WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.602
-My first guest is
an EGOT winner,

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.270
who you can see as
a coach on "The Voice,"

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.907
which airs Mondays at 8:00 p.m.
and Tuesdays at 9:00 p.m.,

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.642
right here on NBC.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.644
Here is John legend.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.581
John, welcome back to the show.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:17.216
I love it. It's you.
It's the piano.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.819
That is a gorgeous piano,
by the way.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.687
-I'm here, man.
I'm happy to be back.

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:24.224
Thanks for having me.
Good to see you.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.858
-I wanted --
I've been wanting to tell you

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:29.028
how much I enjoyed
your performance at

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.530
President Biden's inauguration.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:35.235
You did "Feeling Good,"
Nina Simone.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.970
-Yeah.
-What was that like?

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.174
-Well, I think the whole nation
was feeling this --

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:46.312
or a lot of the nation was
feeling a big sigh of relief

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:50.549
that we were moving on
as a nation

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:54.220
and would have some sanity back
in The White House.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:58.758
And all day -- We had already
planned to sing "Feeling Good,"

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.960
and all day,
I was hearing people say,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.595
"It's a new day,
it's a new day."

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.931
I was like, "I have the perfect
song for this moment."

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:09.002
-"Wait till you hear what
I'm doing." Yeah.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.471
-And, you know,
I love Nina Simone,

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:14.040
and her version
of the song is so iconic.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.610
And I tried my best
to honor her version.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.447
And it was amazing
to do it right there

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.650
in front of the steps of
the Lincoln Memorial,

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.185
you know, where Dr. King gave
his "I Have a Dream" speech,

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:28.554
where so many important moments
in American history

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:29.589
have happened.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.358
And it was an incredible moment.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.994
-Honestly, it was beautiful
and it was just perfect,

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.662
and everyone was,
like, feeling that.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:39.399
It was honestly -- Top to
bottom, that was just great.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.533
-Thank you.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.468
-Something else happened
on Inauguration Day.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:46.472
Joe Biden took over the
@POTUS Twitter handle

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.608
and started following people.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.977
Just a handful of people,
people in the administration --

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.845
-His staff, yeah.
-His staff.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.179
-Just his staff.

00:01:54.179 --> 00:01:56.682
-And then one other person,
and that was your wife,

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.151
Chrissy Teigen.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:01.321 line:0%
He followed -- Chrissy was one
of the people he first followed.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.888 line:0%
It was like --
-Yes.

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:07.393 line:0%
Well, Chrissy prompted him to do
it, because she said,

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.596
you know, the last
president blocked her,

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:13.099
and wouldn't it be so cool

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.434
if Joe Biden
actually followed her.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.236
Not just not blocked her,

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.672
but actually followed her.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.975
-He did it.
-He did it.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:25.077
And she regretted that decision,

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:29.214
because every tweet
she was about to tweet,

00:02:29.214 --> 00:02:30.283
she was like, "Oh, no.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.218
The president
is going to see this."

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:35.187
And so she started
really holding back,

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:37.723
censoring the Chrissy that
we know and love.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.792
-Yeah, respectfully.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.528
-She had to ask President Biden
to unfollow her

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.931
so she could be herself again.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:48.234
And then she just started
cursing a lot afterwards

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:52.671
just to release
all this pent-up energy

00:02:52.671 --> 00:02:54.673
that she was holding back.

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:57.176
-"Look, just please unfollow me.
It's not you. It's me.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:58.244
I love you. Let's just do it."

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.645
And then,
as soon as he unfollowed her,

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:01.047
she's like, "Whew!

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.449
Here we go.
Now we can kick the shoes off.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.584
And there you go."

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.452
Oh, my gosh.
That makes me laugh.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.321
How are the kids, by the way?
You have Luna and Miles.

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:10.656
-They're good.

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:15.928
We're still preschool-podding
here in our playroom.

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:17.997
-What's the
music situation like?

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.498
What are they listening to?

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:25.204
-Luna's main choices are either
Ariana Grande or Selena Gomez,

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:28.107
and Miles' main picks are

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.609
the "Frozen" soundtrack
and daddy.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:34.747
So Miles is, you know,
still requesting my albums.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:38.884
He really likes "I Do"
from my "Bigger Love" album.

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:41.554
And he also loves
the Christmas album,

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.490
so he'll listen to my
Christmas album all year round.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.993
-That Christmas album was a jam.
Dude, I loved that record.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.394
-Thank you.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.196
-Speaking of great albums,
2020 marked

00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:52.865
the 10th anniversary,
believe it or not,

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:56.469
of your Grammy-winning album,
"Wake Up!",

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.371
which you did with The Roots.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:00.272
-Absolutely.
-And I remember this --

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.941
-I remember coming on your show
and promoting it.

00:04:02.941 --> 00:04:06.045
And we had so much fun
making that album.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.947
It was a labor of love.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:09.615
We loved the music.

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:11.550
We loved the artists
that we were covering.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:14.320
And it was just
really powerful material,

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.188
and it was such
a cool album to make

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:17.890
with Questlove
and the whole crew.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.860
-What do you remember most about

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.396
meeting Questlove and the guys
for the first time?

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.599
-Well, I was -- I went to
college in Philadelphia.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.000
I went to UPenn.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.137
And I was a kid from Ohio
with a dream to be

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.906
a musician eventually,
for a living,

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.140
doing what I'm doing now.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.877
But at the time, you know,
The Roots were

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.479
running the music scene
in Philadelphia.

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:41.947
They were hosting "Black Lily"

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:43.448
and all these
different open mics.

00:04:43.448 --> 00:04:46.352
They were producing people like
D'Angelo and Common

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:49.922
and Erykah Badu and Jill Scott
and all these great artists.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.458
And I was just this
up-and-coming young guy

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.260
who went to college at Penn.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:58.130
And I started making my demos
and recording songs

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.932
with some of my friends
in Philly,

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.801
and I wanted Questlove
to hear my music.

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:05.637
So one day, I,
as John Stephens,

00:05:05.637 --> 00:05:07.039
not as John Legend yet --

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.608
I walk up to him after one
of these open mics

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.877
that I had gone to
and I just was like,

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:14.080
"Man, I would love it if you'd
check out my CD."

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.182
And I told him that story when
we were working on "Wake Up!",

00:05:17.182 --> 00:05:19.118
and he had no idea.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.953
He had no remembrance
of that happening,

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.923
which, you know, honestly,
I wouldn't remember it either.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.491
But he didn't remember that.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:28.161
But I did hand him
my demo as John Stephens

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:31.497
probably in like 2000, 2001.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:35.267
And then, 10 years later, we
were making "Wake Up!" together,

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.336
and now here we are now
20 years later.

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:39.839
-When did you go with
John Legend?

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.574
-Well, it was
a nickname that some friends

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:43.409
started calling me
in the studio,

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.244
just guys that
I was collaborating with.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:47.547
The first guy to
call me that was J. Ivy.

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:49.848
He's a spoken-word artist
from Chicago.

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:51.317
I met him through Kanye.

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:52.518
We were all
in the studio together.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:53.886
He just started calling me
"The Legend"

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:54.886
because he thought
I sounded like

00:05:54.886 --> 00:05:57.156
one of our
old-school soul legends.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:06:00.192
And it just caught on with
our little group of friends,

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:01.193
and then they were like,

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:02.428
"We should call
you John Legend."

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:05.531
And it just really
was in our little circle.

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:09.067
And one time,
Kanye put a mix tape out,

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:11.403
and he called me
John Legend on the mix tape.

00:06:11.403 --> 00:06:13.706
And it just started to spread
among more of the people

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.241
that were listening
to our music.

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:17.643
And then, at some point,
I had to decide,

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.612
"Am I going to stick with
John Stephens?"

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:21.447
Which I was perfectly fine with.

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.716
I wasn't looking for
a stage name.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:26.852
"Or am I going to go with
this more audacious name

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:28.120
and call myself a legend

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.723
before I even have
a record deal?"

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.458
-That's a challenge, man.
-That was a challenge.

00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:35.727
And so I was like,
"I know this is a bold move,

00:06:35.727 --> 00:06:38.798
but I'm not going to go into
this expecting to fail.

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:39.898
I'm going to go into it

00:06:39.898 --> 00:06:42.167
hoping that I can try to
live up to this."

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:45.203
And I've spent the rest of
my career trying to do so.

00:06:45.203 --> 00:06:46.839
-Look at you now, bud.

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.841
-Here we are now.
I'm on "Jimmy Fallon"!

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.342
-Come on, now. Come on.

00:06:50.342 --> 00:06:52.344
More with John Legend after
the break, everybody.

00:06:52.344 --> 00:06:54.247
Come on back. Come right back.

